# Alembic migrations

Schema changes are applied with [Alembic](https://alembic.sqlalchemy.org/).

## Setup

Use the project venv and configuration (same as the app):

```bash
export MEIPI_CONFIG_ENV=/path/to/config.env   # optional, default: config.env
uv sync
```

## Commands

```bash
# Apply all pending migrations
alembic upgrade head

# Roll back one revision
alembic downgrade -1

# Show current revision
alembic current

# Create a new revision (autogenerate; requires DB reachable)
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"
```

`alembic/env.py` loads the database URL from `Config` and uses SQLAlchemy metadata from `meipi.indexing.model.Base`.

## Initial content migration

`versions/20260529_move_inhalt_to_filemeta.py` moves `inhalt` and `ts_content` from `documents` to `filemeta`, copies existing text, and adds a GIN index on `filemeta.ts_content`.
